  "interpretation": [
    "The complete 334-body screen covers 7585 poses at 37 sampled orientations for each of four axes: 374941720 pose/orientation cases and 70934920 nonadjacent pair distances. All masks and 49432 summary groups are retained and verified.",
    "483751 of 2533390 body/pose combinations pass the nonadjacent-overlap screen. The other 2049639 remain retained; no native collision behavior or old outcome is rewritten.",
    "Every body has at least one nonoverlapping distal floor-contact pose at every sampled orientation. Reach alone therefore does not establish a useful turning moment.",
    "For both side-roll directions, positive normal-force moments exist on all 334 bodies at 0, 5 and 10 degrees, on 104 at 15, and on none at the samples from 20 through 45 degrees. They return on 149 bodies at 50 and all 334 at 55, using other contacts. This is sampled fixed-pose geometry, not a dynamic barrier proof.",
